Subject: do not re-initialize a thread implicitly after mi_thread_done (backport of upstream 66b6fd4c2)
Fixes: A4, C2 - an allocation on a thread after mimalloc's thread-done hook silently re-initialized the thread, and the new tld, theap and pages were never released
Upstream: fixed upstream in 66b6fd4c2 (2026-11-04), not yet released; this is a backport

In v3.6.1, _mi_thread_done reset the thread's default theap to the
read-only empty theap. A later allocation on that thread (a C++
thread_local destructor or a pthread key destructor of another library
that runs after mimalloc's) found it uninitialized and called
_mi_thread_init, which allocated a fresh tld and theap and pages that no
later thread-done released: at least one 64 KiB page and the bookkeeping
leaked per such thread exit (audit A4, C2).

Upstream's fix, carried over unchanged in logic:
- the thread-done path sets the default theap to a distinct read-only empty
  theap, "unavailable" (process.c), and drops the prim layer's association
  with the freed theap (_mi_prim_thread_associate_default_theap(NULL));
- _mi_thread_is_done() is "the default theap is the unavailable one";
- an allocation on a done thread in the main heap is served from the
  meta-data theap (_mi_meta_zalloc, under its lock; always zeroed), whose
  blocks are ordinary mimalloc blocks, so mi_free and mi_is_in_heap_region
  treat them as any other; first-class heaps return NULL there;
- mi_theap_init no longer re-initializes a done thread; only an explicit
  mi_thread_init does;
- the "theap could not be created" signal, theap_empty_wrong, becomes the
  same unavailable theap, told apart by _mi_thread_is_done().

Adapted to v3.6.1. Upstream had meanwhile moved process data into a
separate metadata area (mi_process_metadata(), dev3 dbab013fe and
a1844f6fd). This patch keeps v3.6.1's layout: the field is
_mi_process.theap_unavailable in mi_process_t (renamed from
theap_empty_wrong), and _mi_theap_is_unavailable compares against its
address. Upstream's documentation and test changes are not vendored. Files:
include/mimalloc/heap/process.h, src/alloc/alloc-generic.c,
src/heap/heap.c, src/heap/process.c.

